// Below each secondary core's stack is a page nothing maps, so a stack that overruns faults instead of writing over
// the next one (the compiled code's own check only knows core 0's stack). Core 0 sees the same tables.
// Worked out: a store to core 2's guard page is a data abort from the same EL (class 0x25 = 37); translation fault at
// level 3, on a write: low 7 bits of ESR_EL1 = WnR (0x40) + DFSC 7 = 0x47. Raven reports FAR_EL1, the guard's address,
// which the test's own line cannot know; the ESR line is exact: EC 0x25 << 26 = 0x94000000, IL 0x02000000, + 0x47.
// expect-fault: ESR_EL1:  0x0000000096000047

import assembly: core_stack_guard

fn test_main() {
    unsafe {
        store64(core_stack_guard(2), 1)
    }
}
